defmodule <%= @web %>.BubbleData do
  @moduledoc """
  The data the pages scaffolded from Bubble show (WTF-420): a page's
  "Type of content" (its thing, from the URL), the data sources of its
  groups, repeating groups and reusable-element instances. The page's
  `Workflows` module (and each reusable element's) lists them in
  `__bubble__(:data)` with one function per source, in the order they read
  each other; this module runs them, keeps what they return in the
  page's `@bubble_data` and reloads it when a record they read changes.

  ## Data access (opt-in)

<%= if @enforced? do %>  The Ash resources have the privacy policies compiled from Bubble
  (`privacy: :enforced`, WTF-423). Every read goes through Ash with the
  current user as the actor (read afresh at each load,
  `<%= @module %>.Privacy.load_actor/1`) and `authorize?: true`: a record
  the user may not view reads as nothing, a field as empty
  (`%Ash.ForbiddenField{}`), and searches run the `:search` action (what
  the user may find in searches). A read the policies refuse outright
  (e.g. logged out, where every rule reads the user) reads nothing, as
  Bubble shows nothing. Pages still load nothing unless the owner opts in,
  the same switch as the workflows':

      config :<%= @app %>, <%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows, data_access: true

  **Not guarded:** a search's own constraints are code, and field policies
  do not apply to code: a constraint on a field the user may not view
  still matches its value (the record itself must still be findable).
  Aggregates over hidden fields are not guarded either.<% else %>  The Ash resources are generated with `privacy: :omit`: **no resource has
  an authorizer**, so every read would return every record to anyone who
  can open the page. Pages load nothing unless the owner opts in, the
  same switch as the workflows':

      config :<%= @app %>, <%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows, data_access: true

  Every read goes through Ash with the current user as the actor and
  `authorize?: true`, which restricts nothing until you add policies.

  **A search that ignores empty constraints can return every record.** A
  page search stating `ignore_empty_constraints: true` drops each
  constraint whose value is empty, as Bubble does (any other empty
  constraint value matches nothing). A signed-in user whose referenced
  field is empty (`X = Current User's Workspace`, with no workspace) or
  whose input is blank gets every record of the type the search can
  read (up to its page size or `:max_items`). A logged-out visitor does
  not: a constraint reading the current user matches nothing for them
  (stricter than Bubble, whose temporary user would drop it). With no
  policies nothing stops this. Before enabling data access, find such
  searches and add policies that limit what each user may read, or
  make the referenced field required, or set the search's
  `ignore_empty_constraints` to false in Bubble where a blank value
  should show nothing; requiring sign-in does not help.<% end %>

  ## What a browser can choose

  Nothing but the page's own state. A page reads only the sources its
  module lists, with their filters fixed in the code; the browser supplies
  input values, custom states and URL parameters (text, pinned into
  filters as values) and, for a page with a type of content, the thing's
  unique ID in the URL path, which must look like a Bubble ID and is read
  through Ash like any other record. No event names a resource, a record
  or a query, and nothing from the browser becomes an atom.

  ## Bounds

  A repeating group shows its first page (its rows times its columns); a
  list with no page size, or a larger one, stops at `:max_items`
  (`config :<%= @app %>, <%= @web %>.BubbleData, max_items: 100`). A
  search's `count` is <%= if @enforced? do %>the number of keys read through `:search`, at most
  `:max_count` (`max_count/0`: Ash's count aggregate under-counts with
  policies that read the user)<% else %>a count query<% end %>. A list of things stored as IDs is
  read by ID, at most the page size capped by `:max_items`. A
  relationship the page's bindings read through a record (its related
  list) reads at most `related_cap/0` records (`:max_items`, at most 100)
  per record, in all when lists nest (a record's tasks' comments share it).

  ## Random order

  A search sorted by Bubble's random sort reads its records ordered by
  the MD5 of each one's primary key and a seed (`random_sort/1`): the
  database orders and limits (the page size, `:max_items`), so a list
  shows a random selection, not the first records shuffled. The seed is
  new on every read, so the order changes whenever the page reads again
  (a change notification included), as Bubble's does on every load. Tests
  fix it (`config :<%= @app %>, <%= @web %>.BubbleData, random_seed:
  "seed"`, set in `config/test.exs`) for a deterministic order. It reads
  no field but the primary key: <%= if @enforced? do %>the policies (and the
  search fields check) apply as to any other search<% else %>nothing to guard<% end %>.

  ## Reactivity

  When loaded (and connected), the page subscribes to one topic per data
  type it searches (a record of that type created, changed or deleted)
  and one per record it holds (`<%= @module %>.Bubble.Changes`, published
  by the resources' `Ash.Notifier.PubSub`), and reloads its data when any
  fires. Only a topic name travels, never a record: the page reads again
  with its own actor.

  The page reads again only when its data is stale (`@bubble_data_stale`):
  a change notification of a topic it subscribes to, a data step of its
  workflows (`<%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows.backend/2`), or a custom state or
  input its workflows changed (they may be search constraints). An event
  whose workflows change none of that reads nothing, and a "do every"
  tick or a scheduled custom event that changes nothing reads nothing.
  Every read clears the flag and takes the change notifications already
  delivered to the page (sent after their writes committed, so the read
  sees them): a workflow's own write and its notification are one read.

  An input change (typing, WTF-475) is narrower: it reads again only the
  sources whose value or search constraints read that input (a source's
  `inputs` in `__bubble__(:data)`) and the sources reading those
  (`reads`, `cell`), transitively; the rest of the page's data stays as
  it is, as read by the same current user: when the user differs from
  the one the page was read as (a changed role, or anything the policies
  read), the whole page reads again. The browser debounces typing
  (`phx-debounce`, 300 ms) and the page coalesces what still arrives into
  one read (`defer/2`). A source listed without `inputs` (scaffolded
  before WTF-475) is read again on any input change, with the rest of the
  page.

  ## Display data (WTF-492)

  An element a "Display data" or "Display list" step set
  (`<%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows.display/8`, kept in `@bubble_displayed`
  until a reset or the page's next load) shows what the step showed, in
  place of its own source (`display:` in its `__bubble__(:data)` entry;
  `read: :displayed` when it has no source of its own). The page kept a
  thing's unique ID only: it is read again through Ash as the current
  user, like any other read, so a workflow never shows what the user may
  not read<%= if @enforced? do %> (a record the policies hide shows nothing, a hidden field is
  empty)<% end %>. A list shows at most its page size, capped by
  `:max_items`.

  ## Unverified Bubble behavior

  To confirm by replay (WTF-358): a page's thing is read from the URL path
  segment after the page name (`/<page>/<unique id>`; Bubble also accepts
  a slug, which is not read here); a search that does not state whether
  it ignores empty constraints is not generated (see
  `docs/page-data.md`); a repeating group's later pages are not loaded;
  "Display data" wins over an element's own source until a reset or the
  page's next load, even when what the source reads changes.
  """

  require Ash.Expr
  require Ash.Query
  require Logger

  import Phoenix.Component, only: [assign: 3]
  import Phoenix.LiveView, only: [connected?: 1]

  alias <%= @module %>.Bubble.Changes
  alias <%= @module %>.Workflows.Runtime
  alias <%= @web %>.BubbleWorkflows

  @id ~r/\A[0-9]{1,20}x[0-9]{1,24}\z/

  @doc "Whether pages may read stored data (the workflows' opt-in)."
  def data_access?,
    do:
      Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, BubbleWorkflows, []), :data_access) == true

  @doc "The most items a list reads (`:max_items`, default 100)."
  def max_items do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_items, 100) do
      n when is_integer(n) and n > 0 -> n
      _ -> 100
    end
  end

  @doc """
  Bubble's random sort (see "Random order"): `query` (or a resource)
  ordered by the MD5
  of the primary key and `random_seed/0`, before its limit. With a
  composite primary key only its first column is hashed: records sharing
  it keep the database's order among themselves.
  """
  def random_sort(query) do
    # A filter of `true` leaves the resource module as it is.
    query = Ash.Query.new(query)
    [pk | _] = Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(query.resource)
    key = Ash.Expr.ref(pk)
    seed = random_seed()

    order = Ash.Expr.calc(fragment("md5(CAST(? AS text) || ?)", ^key, ^seed), type: :string)
    Ash.Query.sort(query, [{order, :asc}])
  end

  @doc """
  The seed of `random_sort/1`: `:random_seed` when configured (text, for
  tests), a new one for every read otherwise.
  """
  def random_seed do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :random_seed) do
      seed when is_binary(seed) and seed != "" -> seed
      _ -> Base.encode16(:crypto.strong_rand_bytes(8))
    end
  end

<%= if @enforced? do %>  @doc """
  The most records a page `count` reads (`:max_count`, default 10_000): a
  count reads the keys of what it counts, and shows this cap past it.
  """
  def max_count do
    case Keyword.get(Application.get_env(:<%= @app %>, __MODULE__, []), :max_count, 10_000) do
      n when is_integer(n) and n > 0 -> n
      _ -> 10_000
    end
  end

<% end %>  @doc """
  The unique ID of a page's thing from the URL path parameter
  (`bubble_thing`): a Bubble ID, else nil.
  """
  def thing_id(%{"bubble_thing" => id}, path)
      when is_binary(id) and byte_size(id) <= 64 and is_binary(path) do
    if List.last(String.split(path, "/", trim: true)) == id and Regex.match?(@id, id), do: id
  end

  def thing_id(_params, _path), do: nil

  # --- loading --------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @doc """
  Loads the page's data into `@bubble_data` (nothing with data access
  off) and, once connected, subscribes to the changes of what it read.
  The data is then current (`@bubble_data_stale` false). <%= if @enforced? do %>The current
  user is read afresh first, unless `actor_fresh?: true` says the caller
  has just done it (`BubbleWorkflows.refresh_actor/1`).<% else %>`opts` is
  for the enforced variant (`actor_fresh?:`), ignored here.<% end %>
  """
  def load(socket, page, opts \\ []) do
    socket =
      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_data_stale, false)
      |> assign(:bubble_data_inputs, MapSet.new())<%= if @enforced? do %>

    socket =
      if data_access?() and not Keyword.get(opts, :actor_fresh?, false),
        do: BubbleWorkflows.refresh_actor(socket),
        else: socket<% else %>

    _ = opts<% end %>

    if data_access?() and connected?(socket) do
      # Notifications already delivered were sent after their writes
      # committed: this read covers them.
      _ = take_changes(Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_topics, MapSet.new()), false)

      {data, by_source} =
        Enum.reduce(BubbleWorkflows.surfaces(page), {%{}, %{}}, fn {scope, module}, acc ->
          load_surface(socket, module, scope, acc)
        end)

      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_data, data)
      |> assign(:bubble_data_actor, data_actor(socket))
      |> assign(:bubble_source_topics, by_source)
      |> subscribe(all_topics(by_source))
    else
      if not data_access?() and connected?(socket) and
           not Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data_warned, false) and sources?(page) do
        Logger.warning(
          "bubble page data not loaded: data access is off " <>
            "(config :<%= @app %>, #{inspect(BubbleWorkflows)}, data_access: true)"
        )
      end

      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_data, %{})
      |> assign(:bubble_data_warned, not data_access?() and connected?(socket))
    end
  end

  @doc """
  A change notification: for a subscribed topic, marks the data stale and
  coalesces a burst into one read.
  """
  def changed(socket, topic) do
    topics = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_topics, MapSet.new())

    cond do
      not data_access?() or not MapSet.member?(topics, topic) -> socket
      is_nil(socket.assigns[:bubble_data_refresh]) -> socket |> mark_stale() |> defer(25)
      true -> mark_stale(socket)
    end
  end

  @doc "Marks the page's data stale: the next `reload/2` reads it again."
  def mark_stale(socket), do: assign(socket, :bubble_data_stale, true)

  @doc """
  Marks the inputs `elements` (Bubble IDs) changed: the next `reload/2`
  reads again only the sources that read them, transitively (WTF-475).
  """
  def mark_inputs(socket, elements) do
    changed = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data_inputs) || MapSet.new()
    assign(socket, :bubble_data_inputs, Enum.into(elements, changed))
  end

  @doc """
  Reads the page's data again only when it is stale, or when a change
  notification of a subscribed topic is already waiting (e.g. the echo of
  a write the event just made outside the workflow runtime). After input
  changes alone (`mark_inputs/2`) it reads only the sources that read
  them.
  """
  def reload(socket, page, opts \\ []) do
    topics = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_topics, MapSet.new())
    waiting? = take_changes(topics, false)
    inputs = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data_inputs) || MapSet.new()

    cond do
      waiting? or Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data_stale, false) -> load(socket, page, opts)
      MapSet.size(inputs) > 0 -> load_inputs(socket, page, inputs)
      true -> socket
    end
  end

  # Reads again the sources that read the changed inputs, and those that
  # read them; keeps the rest, which were read as the same actor. The
  # current user is the one the event read on its way in (never read again
  # here): when it differs from the one the data was read as (a changed
  # role, or anything else the policies read), the whole page reads again.
  # The subscriptions follow what each source last read.
  defp load_inputs(socket, page, changed) do
    socket = assign(socket, :bubble_data_inputs, MapSet.new())
    affected = affected(page, changed)

    cond do
      not (data_access?() and connected?(socket)) or affected == :all ->
        load(socket, page, actor_fresh?: true)

      data_actor(socket) != Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_data_actor) ->
        load(socket, page, actor_fresh?: true)

      MapSet.size(affected) == 0 ->
        socket

      true ->
        data =
          Map.reject(socket.assigns.bubble_data, fn {key, _} ->
            MapSet.member?(affected, elem(key, 1))
          end)

        by_source = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_source_topics, %{})

        {data, by_source} =
          Enum.reduce(BubbleWorkflows.surfaces(page), {data, by_source}, fn {scope, module},
                                                                           acc ->
            load_surface(socket, module, scope, acc, affected)
          end)

        socket
        |> assign(:bubble_data, data)
        |> assign(:bubble_source_topics, by_source)
        |> subscribe(all_topics(by_source))
    end
  end

  # The actor the page's data is read as.
  defp data_actor(socket),
    do: <%= if @enforced? do %>BubbleWorkflows.current_actor(socket)<% else %>socket.assigns[:current_user]<% end %>

  defp all_topics(by_source),
    do: by_source |> Map.values() |> Enum.reduce(MapSet.new(), &MapSet.union/2)

  # The elements of the sources an input change makes read again: those
  # reading a changed input, then those reading them (their data, or the
  # list of the repeating group whose cells they fill), to a fixpoint.
  # `:all` when a source does not say what it reads.
  defp affected(page, changed) do
    sources = for {_scope, m} <- BubbleWorkflows.surfaces(page), s <- sources(m), do: s

    if Enum.all?(sources, &is_list(Map.get(&1, :inputs))) do
      direct =
        for s <- sources,
            Enum.any?(s.inputs, &MapSet.member?(changed, &1)),
            into: MapSet.new(),
            do: s.element

      spread(sources, direct)
    else
      :all
    end
  end

  defp spread(sources, affected) do
    marked = Enum.reduce(sources, affected, &mark_instance(&1, &2))

    next =
      for s <- sources,
          not MapSet.member?(affected, s.element),
          Enum.any?([s.cell | Map.get(s, :reads, [])], &MapSet.member?(marked, &1)),
          into: affected,
          do: s.element

    if MapSet.size(next) == MapSet.size(affected), do: affected, else: spread(sources, next)
  end

  # What reads an instance's thing names the instance as well as its holder.
  defp mark_instance(%{instance: instance, element: e}, set) when is_binary(instance),
    do: if(MapSet.member?(set, e), do: MapSet.put(set, instance), else: set)

  defp mark_instance(_source, set), do: set

  # Takes the change notifications waiting in the page's mailbox; whether
  # one was of a subscribed topic.
  defp take_changes(topics, subscribed?) do
    receive do
      {:bubble, :data_changed, topic} ->
        take_changes(topics, subscribed? or MapSet.member?(topics, topic))
    after
      0 -> subscribed?
    end
  end

  @doc "Debounces input-driven reads; only the latest input values are loaded."
  def defer(socket, delay \\ 150) do
    # A new input supersedes the old timer. Stale queued messages are
    # ignored by pending?/2; notifications leave the pending timer alone.
    ref = make_ref()
    Process.send_after(self(), {:bubble, :data_refresh, ref}, delay)
    assign(socket, :bubble_data_refresh, ref)
  end

  @doc "Whether this is the current (not superseded) refresh timer."
  def pending?(socket, ref), do: not is_nil(ref) and socket.assigns[:bubble_data_refresh] == ref

  @doc """
  Handles the pending refresh: reads when the data is stale (not when a
  read since has covered it); superseded timers do not read. `opts` as
  `load/3`'s.
  """
  def refresh(socket, page, ref, opts \\ []) do
    if pending?(socket, ref) do
      socket
      |> assign(:bubble_data_refresh, nil)
      |> reload(page, opts)
    else
      socket
    end
  end

  defp sources?(page),
    do: Enum.any?(BubbleWorkflows.surfaces(page), fn {_scope, m} -> sources(m) != [] end)

  @doc "The data sources a surface module lists (none for a module scaffolded before WTF-420)."
  def sources(module) do
    module.__bubble__(:data)
  rescue
    FunctionClauseError -> []
  end

  # Every source of the surface, or only those whose element is in `only`;
  # the data, and the topics each source's value needs (by source).
  defp load_surface(socket, module, scope, acc, only \\ nil) do
    {cells, own} =
      module
      |> sources()
      |> Enum.filter(&(is_nil(only) or MapSet.member?(only, &1.element)))
      |> Enum.split_with(& &1.cell)

    acc =
      Enum.reduce(own, acc, fn source, {data, by_source} ->
        ctx = BubbleWorkflows.data_ctx(socket, module, scope, data)
        key_scope = if source.instance, do: BubbleWorkflows.scope(ctx, [source.instance]), else: scope
        key = {key_scope, source.element}

        case value(socket, module, source, key, ctx) do
          {:ok, value} ->
            {Map.put(data, key, value),
             Map.put(by_source, source_id(scope, source), topics(MapSet.new(), source, value))}

          :none ->
            {data, Map.put(by_source, source_id(scope, source), MapSet.new())}
        end
      end)

    # A group in a repeating group's cell holds a value per cell.
    Enum.reduce(cells, acc, fn source, {data, by_source} ->
      items = data |> Map.get({scope, source.cell}) |> List.wrap()
      # The list's own source may have loaded these already (the same
      # relationship for a binding): load only what is missing.
      items =
        Runtime.load_page(
          items,
          source.cell_loads,
          Runtime.root(nil, <%= if @enforced? do %>BubbleWorkflows.current_actor(socket)<% else %>socket.assigns[:current_user]<% end %>),
          related_cap(),
          lazy?: true
        )

      values =
        for {item, i} <- Enum.with_index(items, 1) do
          ctx = BubbleWorkflows.data_ctx(socket, module, scope, data, {item, i})

          case value(socket, module, %{source | loads: []}, {scope, source.element, i}, ctx) do
            {:ok, value} -> {i, value}
            :none -> {i, nil}
          end
        end

      # Load relationships across all cells together, not one query per cell.
      loaded =
        values
        |> Enum.map(&elem(&1, 1))
        |> Runtime.load_page(source.loads, Runtime.root(nil, <%= if @enforced? do %>BubbleWorkflows.current_actor(socket)<% else %>socket.assigns[:current_user]<% end %>), related_cap())

      {data, topics} =
        Enum.zip(Enum.map(values, &elem(&1, 0)), loaded)
        |> Enum.reduce({data, MapSet.new()}, fn {i, value}, {data, topics} ->
          {Map.put(data, {scope, source.element, i}, value), topics(topics, source, value)}
        end)

      {data, Map.put(by_source, source_id(scope, source), topics)}
    end)
  end

  defp source_id(scope, source), do: {scope, source.instance, source.element, source.fun}

  # What a source's element shows: what a "Display data" step showed in it
  # (WTF-492), which wins over its own source until a reset, else its
  # source. An element with no source of its own (`read: :displayed`)
  # shows nothing before a step does (`:none`: an instance's thing is left
  # as the page gave it).
  defp value(socket, module, source, key, ctx) do
    case Map.fetch(Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_displayed) || %{}, key) do
      {:ok, shown} -> {:ok, shown(shown, source, ctx)}
      :error when source.read == :displayed -> :none
      :error -> {:ok, run(module, source, ctx)}
    end
  end

  # A thing a step showed is read again through Ash as the current user
  # (its unique ID is all the page kept): a record the user may not read
  # shows nothing<%= if @enforced? do %>, a field the user may not view is empty<% end %>.
  defp shown({resource, list?, value}, source, ctx) do
    page_size =
      case Map.get(source, :display) do
        %{page_size: n} -> n
        _ -> nil
      end

    ctx
    |> records(resource, value, list?, page_size)
    |> Runtime.load_page(source.loads, Runtime.root(nil, ctx.actor), related_cap())
  rescue
    error ->
      Logger.error(
        "bubble page data #{inspect(source.element)} failed: #{Exception.format_banner(:error, error)}"
      )

      nil
  end

  # One source: its function, then the relationships the page's bindings
  # read through it. A source that fails reads nothing (logged).
  defp run(_module, %{fun: nil}, _ctx), do: nil

  defp run(module, source, ctx) do
    module
    |> apply(source.fun, [ctx])
    |> Runtime.load_page(source.loads, Runtime.root(nil, ctx.actor), related_cap())
  rescue
    error ->
      Logger.error(
        "bubble page data #{inspect(source.element)} failed: #{Exception.format_banner(:error, error)}"
      )

      nil
  end

  # --- reads -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @doc """
  Loads a page expression's relationships with a database-side limit on
  the related lists (`related_cap/0`, as for the sources' own loads).
  """
  def load_value(value, loads, ctx) do
    if data_access?(),
      do: Runtime.load_page(value, loads, Runtime.root(nil, ctx.actor), related_cap()),
      else: value
  end

  @doc """
  The most related records a loaded relationship reads per record:
  `:max_items`, at most 100. Nested lists share it (a list of lists reads
  at most this many in all, not this many per level).
  """
  def related_cap, do: min(max_items(), 100)

  @doc "A page's thing: the record whose unique ID is in the URL, read through Ash."
  def url_thing(ctx, resource) do
    case ctx.thing do
      id when is_binary(id) -> get(resource, id, ctx)
      _ -> nil
    end
  end

  @doc """
  A query's result: `take` is `:all` (at most the page size, capped at
  `max_items/0`), `:first`, `{:item, n}`, `{:limit, n}` or `:count`.
  """
<%= if @enforced? do %>  def read(query, ctx, :count, _page_size) do
    # Counted by reading the records' keys through `:search`, not with
    # `Ash.count/2`: Ash's count aggregate under-counts with policies that
    # read the actor (a record the user finds is not counted). At most
    # `max_count/0` are read; past it the count is that cap, logged.
    [pk] = Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(query.resource)
    cap = max_count()

    query
    |> Ash.Query.select([pk])
    |> Ash.Query.limit(cap + 1)
    |> Ash.read(action: :search, actor: ctx.actor, authorize?: true)
    |> case do
      {:ok, records} when length(records) > cap ->
        Logger.warning(
          "bubble page data: a count of #{inspect(query.resource)} reached :max_count " <>
            "(#{cap}); it shows #{cap}, the true count is larger"
        )

        cap

      {:ok, records} ->
        length(records)

      {:error, error} ->
        failed(query, error)
    end
  end
<% else %>  def read(query, ctx, :count, _page_size) do
    case Ash.count(query, actor: ctx.actor, authorize?: true) do
      {:ok, n} -> n
      {:error, error} -> failed(query, error)
    end
  end
<% end %>
  def read(query, ctx, take, page_size) do
    {offset, limit} =
      case take do
        :all -> {0, cap(page_size)}
        :first -> {0, 1}
        {:item, n} -> {n - 1, 1}
        {:limit, n} -> {0, min(cap(page_size), n)}
      end

    query = query |> Ash.Query.offset(offset) |> Ash.Query.limit(limit)

    case Ash.read(query, <%= if @enforced? do %>action: :search, <% end %>actor: ctx.actor, authorize?: true) do
      {:ok, records} when take in [:first] or is_tuple(take) and elem(take, 0) == :item ->
        List.first(records)

      {:ok, records} ->
        records

      {:error, error} ->
        failed(query, error)
    end
  end

  defp cap(nil), do: max_items()
  defp cap(n) when is_integer(n) and n > 0, do: min(n, max_items())
  defp cap(_), do: max_items()

<%= if @enforced? do %>  # A read the policies refuse outright (e.g. logged out, where every rule
  # reads the user) shows nothing, as in Bubble: not an error.
  defp failed(_query, %Ash.Error.Forbidden{}), do: nil
<% end %>  defp failed(query, error) do
    Logger.error(
      "bubble page data: a read of #{inspect(query.resource)} failed: " <>
        Exception.format_banner(:error, Ash.Error.to_error_class(error))
    )

    nil
  end

  @doc """
  A thing (or list of things) as records of `resource`: records pass,
  Bubble IDs are read through Ash (a list at most its page size, capped by
  `max_items/0`, in its order); anything else is the value itself.
  """
  def records(ctx, resource, value, list?, page_size \\ nil)
  def records(_ctx, nil, value, true, page_size) when is_list(value),
    do: Enum.take(value, cap(page_size))
  def records(_ctx, nil, value, _list?, _page_size), do: value
  def records(_ctx, _resource, nil, _list?, _page_size), do: nil

  def records(ctx, resource, value, true, page_size) when is_list(value) do
    value = Enum.take(value, cap(page_size))
    ids = for id <- value, is_binary(id), do: id

    found =
      if ids == [] do
        %{}
      else
        [pk] = Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(resource)
        filter = [{pk, [in: ids]}]

        resource
        |> Ash.Query.new()
        |> Ash.Query.filter(^filter)
        |> Ash.Query.limit(length(ids))
        |> Ash.read(actor: ctx.actor, authorize?: true)
        |> case do
          {:ok, records} -> Map.new(records, &{Map.get(&1, pk), &1})
          {:error, error} ->
            failed(Ash.Query.new(resource), error)
            %{}
        end
      end

    value
    |> Enum.map(fn
      id when is_binary(id) -> Map.get(found, id)
      record -> record
    end)
    |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)
  end

  def records(ctx, resource, id, _list?, _page_size) when is_binary(id), do: get(resource, id, ctx)
  def records(_ctx, _resource, value, _list?, _page_size), do: value

  defp get(resource, id, ctx) do
    if Regex.match?(@id, id) do
      case Ash.get(resource, id, actor: ctx.actor, authorize?: true, not_found_error?: false) do
        {:ok, record} -> record
        {:error, error} -> failed(Ash.Query.new(resource), error)
      end
    end
  end

  @doc """
  What a filter reads from the current user: the value at `path` (names),
  after loading the relationships `loads`; nil when logged out.
  """
  def actor(ctx, path, loads) do
    ctx
    |> BubbleWorkflows.actor([])
    |> load_value(loads, ctx)
    |> get_path(path)
  end

  defp get_path(value, []), do: value
  defp get_path(nil, _path), do: nil

  defp get_path(value, [name | rest]) when is_map(value),
    do: value |> Map.get(String.to_existing_atom(name)) |> get_path(rest)

  defp get_path(_value, _path), do: nil

  @doc "A pinned filter value: a thing as its ID, things as their IDs."
  def pin(value, :one), do: Runtime.id(value)
  def pin(value, :many), do: Runtime.ids(value)
  def pin(value, _), do: value

  # --- reactivity ------------------------------------------------------------------------

  defp topics(topics, %{topic: nil}, _value), do: topics

  defp topics(topics, %{topic: type} = source, value) do
    topics = if source.read == :query, do: MapSet.put(topics, Changes.topic(type)), else: topics
    record_topics(topics, value, source.loads)
  end

  defp record_topics(topics, values, loads) when is_list(values),
    do: Enum.reduce(values, topics, &record_topics(&2, &1, loads))

  defp record_topics(topics, %{__struct__: resource} = record, loads) do
    type = resource |> Module.split() |> List.last()

    topics =
      case Ash.Resource.Info.primary_key(resource) do
        [pk] -> MapSet.put(topics, Changes.topic(type, Map.get(record, pk)))
        _ -> topics
      end

    Enum.reduce(loads, topics, fn [name | rest], acc ->
      related = Map.get(record, String.to_existing_atom(name))
      record_topics(acc, related, if(rest == [], do: [], else: [rest]))
    end)
  rescue
    _ -> topics
  end

  defp record_topics(topics, _value, _loads), do: topics

  defp subscribe(socket, topics) do
    if connected?(socket) do
      old = Map.get(socket.assigns, :bubble_topics, MapSet.new())

      for topic <- MapSet.difference(topics, old), do: Changes.subscribe(topic)
      for topic <- MapSet.difference(old, topics), do: Changes.unsubscribe(topic)

      assign(socket, :bubble_topics, topics)
    else
      socket
    end
  end
end
